From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:12:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Do not offer eMMC DDR52 on the A733 SD
 controllers

The A733 SD and SDIO controllers (SMHC0, SMHC1) get MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR and
MMC_CAP_3_3V_DDR like every controller with new timings. Seen on the
Radxa Cubie A7S with an eMMC module on a microSD adapter in the SD slot:
the module attaches as a high speed DDR card, every read ends in a data
error and the partition table cannot be read. Without the DDR caps the
same module runs at High Speed SDR, 52 MHz, 4 bit, the mode the boot
loader uses, and reads cleanly. Whether the DDR timing or the 1.8 V
signalling that mmc_select_hs_ddr() switches to with MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR
breaks the transfer is not known.

Do not add the DDR caps by default for these controllers, as is done for
the H5 eMMC. SD and SDIO cards never use them, so the UHS modes of the
slot stay; the A733 eMMC controllers keep DDR52, HS200 and HS400. The
caps are left out before mmc_of_parse(), so a board can still ask for
DDR52 with mmc-ddr-1_8v or mmc-ddr-3_3v.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the SD slot no longer offers DDR52, an SD
card still runs at SDR104 and the eMMC at HS400; an eMMC module on a
microSD adapter was not at hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 5b63310dbf0e..3d888b02d05d 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -379,6 +379,9 @@ struct sunxi_mmc_cfg {
 
 	/* requests go through the host software queue, needs can_wait_busy */
 	bool can_hsq;
+
+	/* card slot: no eMMC DDR52 unless the DT asks for it (mmc-ddr-*) */
+	bool no_mmc_ddr;
 };
 
 struct sunxi_mmc_host {
@@ -2161,6 +2164,7 @@ static const struct sunxi_mmc_cfg sun60i_a733_cfg = {
 	.needs_a12a_init = true,
 	.can_wait_busy = true,
 	.can_hsq = true,
+	.no_mmc_ddr = true,
 };
 
 /* SMHC2 and SMHC3: eMMC, 8 bit, HS400 */
@@ -2439,9 +2443,12 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * use HS DDR mode for their eMMC chips.
 	 *
 	 * We still enable HS DDR modes for all the other controller
-	 * variants that support them.
+	 * variants that support them, except for card slots such as the
+	 * A733 SD controllers, where an eMMC module on a microSD adapter
+	 * fails every read in DDR52.
 	 */
 	if ((host->cfg->clk_delays || host->use_new_timings) &&
+	    !host->cfg->no_mmc_ddr &&
 	    !of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-h5-emmc"))
 		mmc->caps      |= MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR | MMC_CAP_3_3V_DDR;
